What’s not working today

Calls don’t lead to decisions. Feedback is high-level and doesn’t turn into clear requirements.

Actions fall through the cracks. Owners aren’t always clear, tracking is messy, and things get marked “done” without proof.

Too many people in every loop. Risk owners / NOMO are being pulled into routine iterations, which slows everyone down.

Too many hand-offs. ML, Central Service, and Control Owners rely on each other in ways that create waiting and rework.

We already know the “can’t miss” SARs, but they’re not being used as a consistent test / safety baseline each iteration.



---

What to change (simple operating model tweaks)

One place to capture feedback. Control Owners collect input and turn it into clear requirements + what “good” looks like before it comes back to ML / Central Service.

Right people, right meetings.

Weekly working session: ML + Central Service + Control Owners → make decisions and move delivery on.

Monthly checkpoint: bring in risk owners / compliance only for material topics.

Release gate: formal sign-off with an evidence pack.


Tighter action tracking. One action log, one owner per action, due date, and a link to evidence before it’s closed.

Clear hand-offs between teams.

ML brings model results, limits, and scenario coverage.

Central Service brings guardrails, monitoring, and runbooks.

Control Owners bring prioritised asks and acceptance criteria.


Make “must-not-miss” real. Agree a short list of critical SAR patterns and run a non-regression check every release (or document the guardrail/mitigation).
